"TitleBar"|"A bar at the top of a window that displays the title of the window and may contain controls to close, minimize, or maximize the window."  
"MenuBar"|"A horizontal bar that contains menus, typically located at the top of a window."  
"Menu"|"A list of options or commands presented to the user."  
"MenuItem"|"An item within a menu that the user can select to perform an action."  
"ToolBar"|"A bar that contains buttons or icons that perform commands when clicked."  
"StatusBar"|"A horizontal area at the bottom of a window that displays status information."  
"ScrollBar"|"A control that allows the user to scroll the content of a window horizontally or vertically."  
"Grip"|"A control that allows the user to resize a window or pane."  
"Sound"|"An object that represents a sound."  
"Cursor"|"An object that represents the mouse pointer."  
"Caret"|"A blinking cursor that indicates the insertion point in text."  
"Alert"|"A message or notification that alerts the user to a condition."  
"Window"|"A top-level window or a child window."  
"Client"|"The main area of a window where user interaction occurs."  
"PopupMenu"|"A menu that appears upon user interaction, such as right-clicking."  
"SystemMenu"|"A menu that provides system-level commands for a window."  
"Dialog"|"A window used to prompt the user for input or display information."  
"Border"|"A decorative or functional border around a UI element."  
"Grouping"|"A logical grouping of related UI elements."  
"Separator"|"A visual divider between groups of UI elements."  
"ToolTip"|"A small pop-up window that provides descriptive text about a UI element."  
"Application"|"The main application object."  
"Document"|"A document or content area within an application."  
"Pane"|"A section of a window, often used to display different types of information."  
"Chart"|"A graphical representation of data."  
"Dialog"|"A window used to prompt the user for input or display information."  
